    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Luis Robert Jr.** (77.40) standing as our premier offensive anchor. Facing Ranger Suarez, **Luis Robert Jr.** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor (+16%) and a strong dynamic platoon edge (+14%), making him our most reliable play. **Kyle Tucker** (73.09) follows closely behind; while he draws a lower batting order position, his efficiency is boosted by the exploitable matchup against Jackson Kent (5.48 xERA), providing a high floor for production. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (71.84) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.27) round out our top-tier starters, both benefiting from high-value lineup slots and opportunistic matchups against Daniel Lynch IV and Walker Buehler, respectively.\n\nStrategic lineup construction today heavily weights platoon advantages and situational speed. **Coby Mayo** (65.12) is a standout utility play, as the optimizer heavily favors his combination of favorable park dimensions and a strong platoon split against the southpaw Suarez. Conversely, **Jackson Merrill** (47.17) and **Drake Baldwin** (48.99) represent our most precarious starts; **Merrill** is squeezed by an elite hold pitcher in Max Fried, while **Baldwin** faces the stingy Cristopher S\u00e1nchez. **Nasim Nunez** (41.04) was the most difficult bench decision, falling just short of the starting rotation. While **Nunez** offers elite SB upside against the slow delivery of Blake Snell, his bottom-of-the-order projection (-8%) ultimately rendered him too risky compared to the consistent R/RBI potential of our starters.\n\nRisk management remains critical as we navigate several \"Lineup Pending\" designations. All projections rely on assumed batting orders; any late-breaking adjustments to the lineup\u2014particularly for **Gunnar Henderson** or **Heliot Ramos**\u2014could shift their expected value, especially if they drop out of premium run-producing spots. **Wade Meckler** (42.09) occupies the lowest tier of our active lineup; he remains a marginal start strictly to protect game caps while we hope for high-leverage production. We are closely monitoring weather and late scratches, as any shift in these factors could trigger a late-afternoon adjustment to the bench deployment of **Nasim Nunez** or **Liam Hicks**.",
